1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:01,750
So we arrive at the question we left

2
00:00:01,762 --> 00:00:02,650
open at the start.

3
00:00:03,062 --> 00:00:05,275
If the world we see is a simulation,

4
00:00:05,638 --> 00:00:07,050
if the self is a story,

5
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:09,900
and if civilization is skiing toward an abyss,

6
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:11,662
then what is all of this for?

7
00:00:12,075 --> 00:00:13,050
And what is happiness?

8
00:00:13,475 --> 00:00:15,062
Bach's answer begins with suffering.

9
00:00:15,488 --> 00:00:17,912
Suffering happens when your mind cares about things

10
00:00:17,925 --> 00:00:18,912
it cannot change.

11
00:00:19,325 --> 00:00:20,963
It keeps pushing against a wall,

12
00:00:21,262 --> 00:00:22,525
and the wall does not move.

13
00:00:22,938 --> 00:00:23,625
And happiness?

14
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:26,275
The outside world cannot make you happy,

15
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:28,562
because the world itself is neutral.

16
00:00:28,975 --> 00:00:29,862
Rain is not sad.

17
00:00:30,275 --> 00:00:31,300
Money is not joyful.

18
00:00:31,712 --> 00:00:33,525
Only your mind decides what things mean.

19
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,750
That is why Bach offers this line,

20
00:00:36,150 --> 00:00:37,750
one of the most memorable of the whole

21
00:00:37,762 --> 00:00:38,525
conversation:

22
00:00:38,988 --> 00:00:41,050
happiness is a cookie that your brain bakes

23
00:00:41,062 --> 00:00:41,762
for itself.

24
00:00:42,212 --> 00:00:43,975
Think of the cookie a parent promises a

25
00:00:43,988 --> 00:00:46,175
child to get them to eat their vegetables.

26
00:00:46,588 --> 00:00:48,525
Your nervous system does the same thing.

27
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:51,700
Pleasure and satisfaction are signals from your own

28
00:00:51,712 --> 00:00:52,588
operating system,

29
00:00:52,975 --> 00:00:55,362
rewards that keep your primate body fighting,

30
00:00:55,675 --> 00:00:56,825
learning and building.

31
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:58,450
The cookie was never out there.

32
00:00:58,862 --> 00:01:00,050
It was always baked in here.

33
00:01:00,475 --> 00:01:02,800
This also explains why so many people reach

34
00:01:02,962 --> 00:01:05,300
every goal they set and still feel empty.

35
00:01:05,725 --> 00:01:06,337
The promotion,

36
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,675
the house, the bigger number in the bank

37
00:01:08,688 --> 00:01:09,112
account.

38
00:01:09,525 --> 00:01:11,538
Each one delivers a cookie for a moment,

39
00:01:11,862 --> 00:01:13,988
and then the nervous system raises the bar.

40
00:01:14,412 --> 00:01:16,250
The reward was never in the object.

41
00:01:16,662 --> 00:01:17,450
It was a signal,

42
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:19,000
designed to keep you moving.

43
00:01:19,425 --> 00:01:21,450
So stop chasing the cookie in the outside

44
00:01:21,462 --> 00:01:21,863
world.

45
00:01:22,275 --> 00:01:24,650
Instead, try to understand your own software.

46
00:01:25,062 --> 00:01:27,075
Notice the stories your mind tells you,

47
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:28,838
the rewards it dangles,

48
00:01:29,050 --> 00:01:30,250
the fears it runs.

49
00:01:30,675 --> 00:01:32,688
Because once you see the simulation for what

50
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,750
it is, you can stop being a character

51
00:01:34,762 --> 00:01:35,038
in it,

52
00:01:35,425 --> 00:01:36,738
and start becoming its author.

53
00:01:37,150 --> 00:01:39,450
If this conversation bent your mind a little,

54
00:01:39,812 --> 00:01:42,325
watch the full Lex Fridman episode linked in

55
00:01:42,338 --> 00:01:43,025
the description,

56
00:01:43,388 --> 00:01:45,700
and subscribe for more animated breakdowns of the

57
00:01:45,712 --> 00:01:47,538
ideas that shape our future.
